tinosa, and Quercus robur. The landscape is a mosaic of forest, traditionally managed meadows, wooded meadows, fens, and bogs. Local fen vegetation is the Scorpidio-Schoenetum association, dominated by Schoenus ferrugineus, Carex spp., Eriophorum latifolium, Phragmites australis, Molinia caerulea, Juncus subnodulosus, and Menyanthes trifoliata.","sitenotes":null,"geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[22.09672,58.32503]}","altitude":30,"collectionunitid":35115,"collectionunit":null,"handle":"KANNA","unittype":"Core","datasets":[{"doi":["10.21233/9vap-t645","10.21233/9VAP-T645"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calibrated radiocarbon years BP","ageold":9397,"ageyoung":-63}],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":48738,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"A.","contactid":16553,"firstname":"Ansis","familyname":"Blaus","contactname":"Blaus, Ansis"}],"datasettype":"pollen","datasetnotes":null,"recdatecreated":"2020-10-30T21:38:10"},{"doi":[],"agerange":[],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":48736,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"A.","contactid":16553,"firstname":"Ansis","familyname":"Blaus","contactname":"Blaus, Ansis"}],"datasettype":"geochronologic","datasetnotes":null,"recdatecreated":"2020-10-30T21:38:03"},{"doi":["10.21233/8V7W-ZA62"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calibrated radiocarbon years BP","ageold":9397,"ageyoung":-63}],"database":"Neotoma Charcoal Data","datasetid":48737,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"A.","contactid":16553,"firstname":"Ansis","familyname":"Blaus","contactname":"Blaus, Ansis"}],"datasettype":"microcharcoal","datasetnotes":null,"recdatecreated":"2020-10-30T21:38:07"}]}},{"site":{"siteid":27265,"sitename":"Doggerbank","sitedescription":"North Sea, southern slopes of the Doggerbank","sitenotes":null,"geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[3.46167,54.76833]}","altitude":-43,"collectionunitid":35131,"collection